<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">V. P. Menon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1966">1966</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">V. P. Menon was an Indian civil servant who, as secretary of the States Ministry under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vallabhbhai-patel">Vallabhbhai Patel</a>, oversaw the integration of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> after 1947. He drafted the Instrument of Accession and negotiated with rulers to bring more than five hundred states into the new union. He had earlier been constitutional adviser to the last viceroys and helped shape the partition plan of 1947.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Witnesses and historians hold that the riots did not sway the ruler; after negotiations with <b>V. P. Menon</b>, Chithira Thirunal agreed to accede to the Indian Union on 12 August 1947.</blockquote><a href="/empire/travancore">Travancore · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Their rulers had signed Instruments of Accession surrendering defence, foreign affairs and communications to the Dominion of India, but the States Ministry under Vallabhbhai Patel, with its secretary V.P. <b>Menon</b>, judged most of them too small to survive as separate units and pressed them to merge.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-state-of-rajasthan">United State of Rajasthan · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>With British paramountcy at an end, Patel and <b>V. P. Menon</b> persuaded almost all the princes whose states lay within India to accede to it before 15 August, while the states within Pakistan’s borders joined Pakistan.</blockquote><a href="/movement/indian-independence-movement">Indian independence movement · Outcomes</a></li><li><blockquote>Vallabhbhai Patel and <b>V. P. Menon</b> integrated more than five hundred princely states, using force against Hyderabad in 1948.</blockquote><a href="/state/dominion-of-india">Dominion of India</a></li><li><blockquote>In early 1948, under pressure from <b>V. P. Menon</b> and Sardar Patel, the rulers agreed to merge their states into the United State of Kathiawar, inaugurated in February 1948; Junagadh State joined in 1949.</blockquote><a href="/state/saurashtra-state">Saurashtra State</a></li></ul></section>
